        {"type": "prose", "id": "methods", "payload": {"text": "HTTP methods have specific semantics:\n\n- **GET**: fetch a resource. **Safe** (no side effects) and **idempotent** (repeating it gives the same result).\n- **POST**: create a resource. Neither safe nor idempotent.\n- **PUT**: replace a resource. Not safe, but idempotent.\n- **DELETE**: remove a resource. Not safe, but idempotent.\n- **PATCH**: partially update a resource. Not necessarily idempotent.\n\n**Safe** methods can be cached and prefetched. **Idempotent** methods can be safely retried — this matters for unreliable networks."}},
