        {"type": "prose", "id": "intro", "payload": {"text": "The name comes from ship design: a ship's hull is divided into watertight compartments (bulkheads). If one compartment floods, the door is closed and the ship stays afloat. The damage is isolated.\n\nIn software, the same principle applies: if your service calls 3 downstream services (A, B, C), and they all share one thread pool, a failure in A can consume all threads and prevent B and C from being served. A bulkhead gives each downstream its own pool — A's failure only affects A's pool."}},
